{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#998033'> </div> !} DLR: {!</td><td>!} [+ dlr_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_dlr +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#A0A0A0'> </div> !} Other Right Republicans: {!</td><td>!} [+ other_right_republicans_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_other_right_republicans +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#cee817'> </div> !} Regionalists (Lliga/PNV/ERC): {!</td><td>!} [+ regionalists_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_regionalists +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#228B22'> </div> !} Agrarios: {!</td><td>!} [+ agrarios_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_agrarios +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#00008B'> </div> !} [+ ap_name +]: {!</td><td>!} [+ ap_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_ap +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#000043'> </div> !} Monarchists / Traditionalists: {!</td><td>!} [+ other_monarchists_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_other_monarchists +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#000000'> </div> !} [+ jons_name +]: {!</td><td>!} [+ jons_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_jons +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!</table>!}

**Potential coalitions:**

Republican Socialist Conjunction (PSOE + [+ ar_name +] + PRRS + PRR + DLR + Other Left Republicans + Other Right Republicans): [+ republican_socialist_conjunction +]%

Left Republican Coalition (PSOE + [+ ar_name +] + PRRS + Other Left Republicans): [+ left_republican_coalition +]%

Popular Front (PSOE + [+ ar_name +] + PRRS + Other Left Republicans + PCE + Regionalists): [+ popular_front +]%

Right Wing Coalition (PRR + Agrarians + DLR + Other Right Republicans): [+ right_coalition +]%

Left Wing Coalition (PSOE + PCE): [+ left_front +]%

[? if ap_r >= 20 : The rapid rise in ap_name votes is extremely worrying. Many had believed that the party was marginal; now, some of us consider it to be the greatest threat to the republic. ?]

[? if anti_democratic_coalition >= 50 : Together, the anti-democratic PCE, ap_name, monarchists and jons_name have a majority in the Cortes. A stable governing majority will be almost impossible. ?]

There are some potential coalition arrangements.











































####################################################################################### COALICIONES

@coalition_menu

- @republican_socialist_conjunction
- @left_republican_coalition
- @popular_front
- @right_coalition
- @left_coalition
- @far_right_coalition



########################################## CONJUNCION REPUBLICANA SOCIALISTA

@republican_socialist_conjunction
title: We can form a Republican-Socialist Conjunction.
view-if: republican_socialist_conjunction >= 50 and grand_coalition_failed == 0
subtitle: PSOE + PRR + PRRS + [+ ar_name +] + DLR + Other minor republican parties ([+ republican_socialist_conjunction +]%)
on-arrival: in_republican_socialist_conjunction = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; in_left_republican_coalition = 0; in_emergency_government = 0; in_psoe_majority = 0; in_minority_government = 0
go-to: grand_coalition_first if n_elections <= 1; grand_coalition_psoe_lead if (psoe_r >= 30 and largest_party == "PSOE" and n_elections > 1); grand_coalition_z_lead if (prr_r + dlr_r) > 30 and n_elections > 1; grand_coalition_ar_lead if (psoe_r < 30 and prr_r + dlr_r < 30 and n_elections > 1)

@grand_coalition_first
view-if: republican_socialist_conjunction >= 50
on-arrival: psoe_in_government = 1; pro_republic += 5; chancellor = "Alcala-Zamora"; chancellor_party = "DLR"; foreign_minister_party = "PRR"; interior_minister_party = "DLR"; justice_minister_party = ar_name; labor_minister_party = ar_name; reichswehr_minister_party = ar_name; economic_minister_party = "Regionalists"; finance_minister_party = "PRRS"; agriculture_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_works_minister_party = "PRRS"; leverage = 25 if leverage >= 25; in_republican_socialist_conjunction = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; in_left_republican_coalition = 0; in_emergency_government = 0; in_psoe_majority = 0; in_minority_government = 0
go-to: ministries

The Republican-Socialist Conjunction is able to get a majority in the Constituyent Cortes due to the disorganization of the monarchical forces. Being a Constituyent Election, Alcala-Zamora remains President of the Provisional Government. Until the Constitution is made, the Head of the State remains in Vacancy. Now, we have to pick our ministries.


@grand_coalition_z_lead
go-to: grand_coalition_z_lead_2 if prr_relation >= 30; grand_coalition_fail if prr_relation < 30

There are enough votes to form a majority coalition consisting of the PSOE, Radical Republicans (PRR), Socialist Radical Republicans (PRRS), Azana's ([+ ar_name +]), Liberal Republican Right (DLR), and other minor republican parties. Given our rather weak electoral performance, [? if psoe_no_confidence = 1 : and our previous vote of no confidence against the government, ?][? if no_confidence_against_psoe = 1 : and the vote of no confidence against us, ?] President [+ President +] has asked the Radical Republican Party (PRR) to take the lead role in forming a government.

@grand_coalition_z_lead_2

The candidate is likely to be [+ prr_leader +] [? if chancellor = "Lerroux" and prr_leader = "Lerroux" : again. ?][? if chancellor != "Lerroux": . ?] He is known for his populism and anti-clericalism, being on the right wing of its party. [? if austerity >= 2 : Due to the government's austerity policies, many of our members are reluctant to participate in this coalition again. Some support a "toleration" arrangement in which we will provide outside support to prevent the far-right from either entering government or calling a successful no-confidence vote. Others support entering into pure opposition, and letting the right do what it wishes. ?]

[+ prr_leader +] is not opposed to a coalition with us. Alternatively, we could enter a "toleration" agreement.

- @join_bruning: Join the [+ prr_leader +] coalition.
- @bruning_oppo: Join the opposition.
- @toleration_bruning: We will "tolerate" a minority government.

@join_bruning
view-if: republican_socialist_conjunction >= 50
on-arrival: psoe_in_government = 1; chancellor = "Lerroux" if prr_leader == "Lerroux"; chancellor = "Martinez Barrios" if prr_leader == "Martinez Barrios"; chancellor_party = "PRR"; foreign_minister_party = "PRR"; interior_minister_party = "DLR"; justice_minister_party = ar_name; labor_minister_party = ar_name; reichswehr_minister_party = ar_name; economic_minister_party = "Regionalists"; finance_minister_party = "PRRS"; agriculture_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_works_minister_party = "PRRS"; leverage = 25 if leverage >= 25; in_republican_socialist_conjunction = 1; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; in_left_republican_coalition = 0; in_emergency_government = 0; in_psoe_majority = 0; in_minority_government = 0
go-to: ministries

[+ chancellor +] welcomes us into his new cabinet. Now, we have our pick of ministries.

@bruning_oppo
on-arrival: psoe_in_government = 0; psoe_toleration = 0; chancellor = "Lerroux" if prr_leader == "Lerroux"; chancellor = "Martinez Barrios" if prr_leader == "Martinez Barrios"; chancellor_party = "PRR"; foreign_minister_party = "PRR"; interior_minister_party = "DLR"; justice_minister_party = ar_name; labor_minister_party = ar_name; reichswehr_minister_party = ar_name; economic_minister_party = "Regionalists"; finance_minister_party = "PRRS"; agriculture_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_works_minister_party = "PRRS"; grand_coalition_failed = 1

By refusing to join the grand coalition or tolerating it, we essentially throw the balance of government to the right wing. [? if right_coalition >= 50 : There are enough votes to form a right-wing coalition. ?][? if far_right_coalition >= 50 : There are enough votes to form a right-wing coalition alongside the [+ ap_name +]. ?][? if right_coalition < 50 : There are not enough votes to form a right-wing coalition. This means that there is no route to a majority coalition. ?]

If we do not at least "tolerate" the government, there will be new elections in a few months. And it is not at all clear that we will do any better in the next election.

- @join_bruning: Join the Brüning coalition.
- @toleration_bruning: We will tolerate Brüning after all.
- @brauns_dilemma
- @far_right_coalition
- @right_coalition_2
- @new_elections: New elections, it is!

@toleration_bruning
choose-if: republican_socialist_conjunction >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: The parties supporting the PRR do not have a majority.
on-arrival: psoe_in_government = 0; minority_government = 1; chancellor = "Lerroux" if prr_leader == "Lerroux"; chancellor = "Martinez Barrios" if prr_leader == "Martinez Barrios"; chancellor_party = "PRR"; foreign_minister_party = "PRR"; interior_minister_party = "DLR"; justice_minister_party = ar_name; labor_minister_party = ar_name; reichswehr_minister_party = ar_name; economic_minister_party = "Regionalists"; finance_minister_party = "PRRS"; agriculture_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_instruction_minister_party = "PRRS"; public_works_minister_party = "PRRS"; pro_republic -= 4; middle_ar -= 5; middle_prrs -= 5; middle_ap += 10; rural_ap += 5; in_republican_socialist_conjunction = 0; in_popular_front = 0; in_left_front = 0; in_left_republican_coalition = 0; in_emergency_government = 0; in_psoe_majority = 0; in_minority_government = 0

We have decided to tolerate [+ chancellor +]'s government. This means that we will vote against no-confidence votes to make sure they fail, but also that we will not be directly participating as ministers in the government. Thus, we can prevent a new election and stop the far right from entering government.


@new_elections
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 3;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 3;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}
if (Q.chancellor_party == "PRR") {
    Q.prr_relation -= 5;
    Q.dlr_relation -= 5;
}
Q.pro_republic -= 8;
Q.workers_psoe -= 5;
Q.middle_psoe -= 5;
Q.rural_psoe -= 5;
Q.catholics_psoe -= 3;
Q.middle_ar -= 8;
Q.middle_prrs -= 8;
Q.rural_ap += 5;
Q.workers_ap += 5;
Q.middle_ap += 6;
Q.unemployed_ap += 5;
// Thresholds are kind of arbitrary - adjusted because of negative economic effects on pro_republic
if (Q.pro_republic < 45 && Q.pro_republic >= 36) {
    Q.workers_psoe -= 6;
}
if (Q.pro_republic < 36) {
    // TODO: if you pursue a consistently revolutionary course, you might avoid this? But you might also cause a coalition between Hitler and the Center.
    Q.ar_relation -= 5;
    Q.prrs_relation -= 5;
    Q.middle_psoe -= 5;
    Q.rural_pce += 5;
    Q.catholics_pce += 3;
    Q.workers_pce += 12;
    Q.middle_ap += 8;
    Q.rural_ap += 8;
    Q.unemployed_ap += 8;   
}
if (Q.far_right_coalition >= 50) {
    Q.mf_strength += 30;
    Q.rc_strength += 20;
    Q.coup_progress += 3;
}
!}

There is no path to a workable Cortes majority or minority government. The next elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

The people's faith in democracy is shaken by this ordeal. Of course, the [+ ap_name +] are exploiting the instability to claim that this republic is unworkable, and that Spain needs a strong leader.

@grand_coalition_fail
