Since the remaining bourgeois and right-wing parties cannot form a tolerable governing agreement, new elections have been called for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +]. The previous chancellor has resigned, and has been replaced by Manuel Azana, of the [+ ar_name +], as a consensus figure until next elections. 

We are seen as responsible for the failure to form a government, and many of our middle-class and even some working-class supporters have deserted the party.

@grand_coalition_ar_lead
go-to: grand_coalition_ar_lead_2 if ar_relation >= 30; grand_coalition_fail if ar_relation < 30

There are enough votes to form a majority coalition consisting of the PSOE, Radical Republicans (PRR), Socialist Radical Republicans (PRRS), Azana's ([+ ar_name +]), Liberal Republican Right (DLR), and other minor republican parties. Given our rather weak electoral performance, [? if psoe_no_confidence = 1 : and our previous vote of no confidence against the government, ?][? if no_confidence_against_psoe = 1 : and the vote of no confidence against us, ?] President [+ President +] has asked Azana ([+ ar_name +]) to take the lead role in forming a government as a consensus figure.

@grand_coalition_ar_lead_2

The candidate will be Azana [? if chancellor = "Azana": again. ?][? if chancellor != "Azana": . ?] He is known for his progressism and anti-clericalism. [? if austerity >= 2 : Due to the government's austerity policies, many of our members are reluctant to participate in this coalition again. Some support a "toleration" arrangement in which we will provide outside support to prevent the far-right from either entering government or calling a successful no-confidence vote. Others support entering into pure opposition, and letting the right do what it wishes. ?]

Azana looks to form a coalition with us. Alternatively, we could enter a "toleration" agreement.

- @join_azana: Join the Azana's coalition.
- @azana_oppo: Join the opposition.
- @toleration_azana: We will "tolerate" a minority government.

